      "text": "To solve for the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\):\n\n1. **Calculate the remainder of \\(-3737\\) when divided by 8**:\n   \\[\n   -3737 \\div 8 = quot9 \\text{ with a remainder} \\text{ = remainder}\n   \\]\n   Compute the initial integer division:\n   \\[\n   -3737 \\div 8 = -467.125\n   \\]\n   The integer part of the division is \\(-467\\).\n\n   So, the division steps are:\n   \\[\n   -3737 = -467 \\times 8 + remainder\n   \\]\n   Solving for the remainder:\n   \\[\n   remainder = -3737 - (-467 \\times 8)\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\( 467 \\times 8 \\):\n   \\[\n   467 \\times 8 = 3736\n   \\]\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   remainder = -3737 - 3736 = -7473\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by 8 is \\(7\\):\n   \\[\n   -3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Verify the conditions**:\n   The equivalence is given by \\( n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8} \\), and the interval \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) matches:\n   \\[\n   0 \\le 7 \\le 7\n   \\]\n   Thus, \\( n = 7 \\) satisfies the conditions.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
